  "title": "Almost-everywhere segment bound for differences of a Lipschitz function",
  "statement": "Let n ∈ ℕ and u : ℝⁿ → ℝ (ℝⁿ = Euclid n) Lipschitz. Then for Lⁿ⊗Lⁿ-almost every (x, y) ∈ ℝⁿ × ℝⁿ: (u(x) − u(y))² ≤ ‖x − y‖²·∫_0^1 ‖Du((1 − t)y + tx)‖² dt. Here Du = fderiv ℝ u with the operator norm, and the integral is the interval integral from 0 to 1.",
